st-wl-paste(1) -- wl-paste that sanitizes the clipboard on read
==============================================================

<!--
# Copyright (C) 2026 - 2026 ENCRYPTED SUPPORT LLC <adrelanos@whonix.org>
# See the file COPYING for copying conditions.
-->

## SYNOPSIS

`st-wl-paste` [<WL-PASTE-OPTION>...]

## DESCRIPTION

st-wl-paste is a drop-in replacement for `wl-paste`(1) (Wayland) that filters the
clipboard text through `sclip`(1) as it is read. Every argument is forwarded
verbatim to `wl-paste`, so native options such as `--primary` or `--no-newline`
work unchanged.

By default the strip is strictest (printable ASCII only). Set the environment
variable `SCLIP_MODE=unicode` to keep printable non-ASCII instead.

Compose it like the original, sanitizing one or both sides:

    st-wl-paste | st-wl-copy
    st-wl-paste | wl-copy

## ENVIRONMENT

  * `SCLIP_MODE`:
    When set to `unicode`, keep printable non-ASCII (passes `--unicode` to
    `sclip`). Any other value (or unset) is the default ASCII-only strip.

## EXIT STATUS

The exit status of the underlying `wl-paste` | `sclip` pipeline; 127 if
`wl-paste` is not installed.

## SEE ALSO

`st-wl-copy`(1), `st-xclip`(1), `sclip`(1), `wl-paste`(1)
